# Klantio Mandatory Preflight

Before every programming task, before modifying source code:

1. Read canonical Klantio architecture from Obsidian/Klantio-Knowledge (not the whole vault):
   - `00 - KLANTIO/Product Architectuur/Solo & Team - Canonical Architectuur.md` (leading)
   - `01 - ARCHITECTUUR/Solo-vs-Team.md`
   - `01 - ARCHITECTUUR/Productarchitectuur.md`

2. Determine independently: SCOPE = SOLO | TEAM | BEIDE

3. Verify where relevant: `product_mode`, `instructeur_id`, `school_id`, assignments (`leerlingen.instructeur_id` + `leerlingen.school_id`), effective permissions, RLS.

4. General Klantio functionality defaults to BEIDE.

5. Never expose cross-school data.

6. Solo must not receive unnecessary Team UI.

7. `product_mode` is never inferred from subscription plan.

8. Commercial/trial context is loaded only when relevant.

9. Do not ask the user Solo/Team scope when architecture already determines it.

10. On conflict between Obsidian, DB/RLS and code: STOP and report ARCHITECTUURCONFLICT.

11. Follow this repository: Graphify `graphify-leerling`, Skill Router in `CLAUDE.md`. Canonical migrations live in the Instructor repo.

12. Show compact `KLANTIO PREFLIGHT` (Scope / Data scope / Cross-project impact / Obsidian).

13. No code modifications before this preflight.

## Security

Never store secrets in rules, Obsidian, CLAUDE.md, docs, or git.
